    <ObjectList>
      <MultilingualText ID="1" CompositionName="Comment">
        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualTextItem ID="2" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>Station health, written by OB86 (RackOrStationFailure). Until this existed, an ET200SP could lose power and nothing in the system noticed: the valves on it simply stopped answering while the HMI carried on showing their last known positions as though they were live. Stale data presented as current is the actual hazard here, more than the loss of control - an operator plans a ballast transfer on positions that stopped being true ten minutes ago. The three hardware identifiers are data rather than code so that re-adding a station in TIA, which reassigns them, does not require an SCL edit. Read the current values off the SYSTEM DIAGNOSTICS screen: every device tile shows its identifier beneath the name.</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
    </ObjectList>
